// expect: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// A LIST PATTERN'S REST IS CUT: binding `...rest` calls the runtime's `slice`
// for the elements past the prefix, so the match performs what `slice`
// performs — `Memory + Alloc` — and a fn declaring `!Alloc` around it is a
// false absence proof. The allocation audit found sixteen such rests in the
// wheel on its first run (Hβ.effects.allocation-audit-at-the-settle-point).
fn after_first(xs) with !Alloc = match xs {
  [_, ...rest] => len(rest),
  _ => 0,
}

fn main() = after_first([1, 2, 3])
